        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T17:35:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So we should guarantee that the TLB will be flushed eventually when another VM is created with the same EPT root, right?\n\nIIUC we don\u0027t need to flush the TLB immediately when creating another VM, we just need to flush it when loading any vCPU of this VM into a physical CPU which may have stale TLB entries from the old VM.\n\nAnd IIUC we do that in this code in vmx_vcpu_load_vmcs():\n\n```\n\t\t/*\n\t\t * Flush all EPTP/VPID contexts, the new pCPU may have stale\n\t\t * TLB entries from its previous association with the vCPU.\n\t\t */\n\t\tkvm_make_request(KVM_REQ_TLB_FLUSH, vcpu);\n```\n\ni.e. whenever we load any vCPU of any VM onto any pCPU, we flush all TLB entries on this pCPU, not just for a particular EPT root.\n\nAm I missing something?",
      "parentUuid": "77d0f88b_30fd23e3",
